468},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n \n \nThis memo contains details about the income tax and the Social Security contribution rates for \n2024/2025 and the increase in UC benefit rates from 07.4.24. The rates are introduced by the \nSocial \nSecurity Benefits Uprating Order 2025  \n   \n(SI 2025/295) and\n the \nSocial Security (Contributions) (Rates, \nLimits and Thresholds Amendments, National Insurance Funds Payments and Extension of Veterans \nRelief) Regulations 2025\n (SI 2025/288) and the \nSocial Security Benefit Uprating Regulations 2025 \n(SI \n2025/352).This memo also contains guidance on the \nEmployment Rights (Increase of Limits) Order \n2025\n (SI 2025/348) and the \nSocial Security (Contributions)(Re-rating) Consequential Amendment \nRegulations 2025 (SI 2025/318)\n which come into effect from 07.04.24.","tree_line_end":528,"tree_line_start":473},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"UPRATING","tree_line_end":532,"tree_line_start":529},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"Benefit rates","tree_line_end":536,"tree_line_start":533},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2. \n \nNew rates of UC will apply from the first day of the first assessment period which commences on or \nafter 07.04.25. DMs can find the new rates in the \nbenefit uprating schedule\n and benefit desk aids and \nshould bear them in mind when reading examples in the ADM that contain benefit rates.","tree_line_end":549,"tree_line_start":537},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Housing costs non-dependant contribution","tree_line_end":553,"tree_line_start":550},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3. \n \nWhere a non-dependant lives with the claimant, a contribution may be appropriate. The contribution is \nmade in the form of a deduction from the allowable housing costs\n1\n. Where applicable \n(see \nADM F3140\n)\n \nthe rate of deduction is £93.02","tree_line_end":572,"tree_line_start":554},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nUC Regs, Sch 4, para. 14(1)","tree_line_end":581,"tree_line_start":573},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Earned income – work allowance","tree_line_end":585,"tree_line_start":582},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"4. \n \nThe appropriate work allowance is\n1","tree_line_end":594,"tree_line_start":586},{"depth":2,"role":"Table","text":"1.\n \n Higher work allowance\nAmount\nSingle claimant - \n \nresponsible for a child or qualifying young person and/or \nhas limited capability for work\n£684\nJoint claimants - \n \nresponsible for one or more children or qualifying young \npersons and/or where one or both have limited capability \nfor work\n£684\n2.\n \n Lower work allowance\n \nSingle claimant - \n \nresponsible for one or more children or qualifying young \npersons and/or has limited capability for work\n£411\nJoint claimants - \n \nresponsible for one or more children or qualifying young \npersons and/or where one or both have limited capability \nfor work\n£411","tree_line_end":823,"tree_line_start":595},{"depth":3,"role":"TR","text":"1.\n \n Higher work allowance\nAmount","tree_line_end":625,"tree_line_start":602},{"depth":4,"role":"TD","text":"1.\n \n Higher work allowance","tree_line_end":616,"tree_line_start":604},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"1.\n \n Higher work allowance","tree_line_end":616,"tree_line_start":608},{"depth":4,"role":"TD","text":"Amount","tree_line_end":625,"tree_line_start":617},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"Amount","tree_line_end":625,"tree_line_start":621},{"depth":3,"role":"TR","text":"Single claimant - \n ","tree_line_end":647,"tree_line_start":626},{"depth":4,"role":"TD","text":"Single claimant - ","tree_line_end":638,"tree_line_start":628},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"Single claimant - ","tree_line_end":638,"tree_line_start":632},{"depth":4,"role":"TD","text":" ","tree_line_end":647,"tree_line_start":639},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":647,"tree_line_start":643},{"depth":3,"role":"TR","text":"responsible for a child or qualifying young person and/or \nhas limited capability for work\n£684","tree_line_end":667,"